contributors (https://github.com/cipansor/crateworks).

The identifier rules, both the national ones and the international ones
(ISIN, CUSIP, FIGI, LEI, BIC, GRid, ISSN, ISRC, IMEI, ISMN, ISNI, CAS RN, the
ISO 11649 creditor reference, the MAC address and the ISIL), and the check-digit
algorithms (Luhn, the ISO 7064 family, Damm and Verhoeff), were cross-checked
against the python-stdnum library by Arthur de Jong and contributors
(https://arthurdejong.org/python-stdnum/), which is distributed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later. The rules themselves encode
each authority's published specification; this crate is an independent
reimplementation for Rust and shares no code with it.

